hub.com/users/penninghlhd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penninghlhd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penninghlhd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penninghlhd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penninghlhd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penninghlhd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penninghlhd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penninghlhd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penninghlhd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-17T08:48:08Z","updated_at":"2024-12-17T08:48:08Z","body":"As I said before, I do not have the time to fix the conflicts myself at the moment. Also the conflicts arise largely from the recently added support for Linux which also implied some interface changes.\r\n\r\nI propose someone in charge of arcitecture for the Camera feature should redefine the interface in order to resolve the conflicts properly.\r\n\r\nIn my opinion the main issues to be addressed should be:\r\n\r\n1. Do we define a feed for each combination of supported dimension and data format and let the user choose to most appropriate feed (as I implemented in this PR), or do we define a feed per camera and make the preferred dimension and data format configurable via CameraTexture?\r\n2. Do we use (predefined/custom) shaders to render the different image formats (YUV, N21, etc) by the GPU via CanvasTexture channels (as I implmented in this PR), or do we use CPU based conversion to RGB format supported by the default renderer.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2547833862/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},